<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Satgaon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saptagram</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Satgaon, ancient Saptagram, was a river port on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saraswati">Saraswati</a>, a branch of the Hooghly, in the Hooghly district of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>. From the 13th to the 16th century it was the chief port of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and a seat of governors and mints, trading with South-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and later the Portuguese. As the Saraswati silted up in the 16th century, its trade moved to the town of Hooghly.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/satgaon.jpg" alt="Satgaon" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pinaki1983 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A6%B8%E0%A6%AA%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%97%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%AE_%E0%A6%B9%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%97%E0%A6%B2%E0%A7%80_%E0%A6%A4%E0%A7%87_%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%B0%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%AE%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A6%B8%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%B8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%A4%E0%A7%80_%E0%A6%A8%E0%A6%A6%E0%A7%80%E0%A6%B0_%E0%A6%85%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%B8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A5%E0%A6%BE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
